{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Opened a sourced question about a public interface promise. ConfigurationStore documents StoreConfiguration as invoked once a log entry containing a configuration change is committed, and BatchingFSM documents that ApplyBatch receives LogConfiguration entries. runFSM chooses one path per FSM: applySingle calls StoreConfiguration for a configuration entry, and applyBatch never does, so an FSM that implements both interfaces should only ever see configuration changes through ApplyBatch. A construction run of the probe bears that out and is the reason the question is worth a retained execution: the ConfigurationStore-only FSM recorded the configuration change through StoreConfiguration, while the FSM implementing both recorded none and saw the same entries in ApplyBatch. The probe builds each case with the repository's own cluster helper, triggers one configuration change by moving an existing voter's address, and reports the callback counts. Execution is requested; the event values decide the question rather than this rationale.\\\"),\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"batching_fsm_iface\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"fsm.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":54,\\\"end_line\\\":69,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"config_store_iface\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"configuration.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":44,\\\"end_line\\\":52,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"fsm_single_apply\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"fsm.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":95,\\\"end_line\\\":118,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"fsm_batch_apply\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"fsm.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":120,\\\"end_line\\\":170,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@batch_fsm_config_store\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"When an application FSM implements both BatchingFSM and ConfigurationStore, is StoreConfiguration invoked for a committed configuration change as its documentation states, or is the change delivered only through ApplyBatch?\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm_iface\\\",\\\"config_store_iface\\\",\\\"fsm_single_apply\\\",\\\"fsm_batch_apply\\\"],\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"runFSM's applySingle calls StoreConfiguration for LogConfiguration entries only when the FSM is not a BatchingFSM, because applyBatch takes over entirely once batchingEnabled is true and handles configuration entries by sending them to ApplyBatch; the batching path contains no StoreConfiguration call, so the promise is not kept for an FSM that implements both interfaces.\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"The callback counts of an FSM implementing both interfaces compared with an FSM implementing only ConfigurationStore, after one configuration change is committed through the leader.\\\"}],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@batch_fsm_config_store\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm_iface\\\",\\\"config_store_iface\\\",\\\"fsm_single_apply\\\",\\\"fsm_batch_apply\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Two cases, each a three-voter cluster built with the repository's own cluster helper whose FSMs share a recorder: one case where the FSM implements FSM and ConfigurationStore, and one where it also implements BatchingFSM. Each case triggers a single configuration change by moving an existing voter's address, waits until the change reaches the FSM, and reports how many times StoreConfiguration and ApplyBatch were called with configuration entries.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Moving an existing voter's address is a legal configuration change that nextConfiguration accepts for a voter, and with three voters the entry commits on the leader and one other node before the moved address matters.\\\",\n    \\\"The recorder is shared across the cluster's FSMs only to answer whether the callback is ever invoked anywhere in the cluster; per-node attribution is not needed for that question.\\\",\n    \\\"The cluster helper builds in-memory transports and stores, so no external service is involved.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whether an application should rely on StoreConfiguration when it also batches, and any behaviour of ApplyBatch ordering or responses.\\\"]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case calls MakeClusterCustom with three peers, bootstrapping and the in-memory test configuration, and a MakeFSMFunc that returns either an FSM implementing FSM and ConfigurationStore or one that also implements ApplyBatch; both record every callback into a shared recorder. The case emits assurance_config_store_setup, picks a follower, calls leader.AddVoter with that follower's ID and a new address (so that the configuration changes without removing anyone), waits up to five seconds for either callback counter to become non-zero, waits a further 200ms, and emits assurance_config_store_result with the call counts. The harness is TestAssuranceConfigurationStoreWithBatching.\\\"),\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_setup\\\"}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"store_configuration_calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"An FSM implementing both interfaces: whether the documented StoreConfiguration callback arrives for a committed configuration change.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"apply_batch_config_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The same case: whether the configuration entry was delivered through ApplyBatch instead.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"store_configuration_calls\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: an FSM implementing only ConfigurationStore does receive the callback, so the difference is the batching interface and not the trigger.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_config_store_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"apply_batch_config_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"batching_fsm\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the non-batching FSM sees no ApplyBatch call at all.\\\"}]}}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_cod